                <pb facs="0338" n="228" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg228"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">660p.11241/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Latvia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sussdorff</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-12T16:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 12,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 12—11:20
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>87. Department’s 539, July 10th, last paragraph. Have received note from Latvian
                    Foreign Office stating as from October 15, 1928, United States consular officers
                    of career in Latvia shall enjoy on the basis of reciprocity the privilege of
                    free entry of personal property during their incumbency. Please telegraph date
                    on which similar privileges will be accorded to Latvian consuls of career in the
                    United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sussdorff</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
